    "stale_rate": "active claims whose evidence hash mismatched during the pre-registered drift set (docs included), pooled across fixtures: Σ stale_during / Σ (active_total × drift files). `stale_rate_worst` is the worst single-file case.",
    "false_claim_rate": "flagged claims / eligible claims. A claim is eligible if it is (a) authored by lore:ingest (checked against a fresh `ingest --dry-run` re-derivation), (b) has file/test evidence (hash re-check), (c) declares a dependency or script (checked against the actual package.json — `pkg_manifest`), or (d) exposes a route (route path + verb grepped from the referenced source — `route_source_grep`). The checks used are listed per fixture in results[].metrics.false_claim_checks_used. If 0 claims are eligible the scenario FAILS — the rate can never be 0 by construction.",
    "conflict_rate": "aborted merge attempts / all merge attempts. The protocol replays a deliberate conflicting (subject,predicate) per round (`--replays` widens the denominator); no synthetic clean merges. SPEC's < 10% target is calibrated on 20 real-session replays; a deliberate-conflict replay is expected to exceed it until enough rounds accumulate.",
    "revert_correctness": "after `lore revert <merge-commit>`, `lore diff <pre-merge> agent/<session>` shows 0 added / 0 removed (exact active-set snapshot equality) AND, when the fixture exposes a runnable test suite, the suite passes after revert. When the suite cannot run in the offline eval copy the phase is recorded as SKIPPED with the explicit reason — never counted as success.",
    "token_savings": "chars/4 token proxy. Baseline per question = bytes of the referenced repo files you would have to read. Memory per question = bytes of the real `lore search <question> --files <refs> --json` subprocess output. The JSON envelope (score, score reasons, evidence per hit) deliberately over-counts: it includes presentation metadata beyond the SPEC §9 claim-blue budget, so savings are a conservative LOWER bound. Questions with 0 search hits score 0 savings (the agent must read the files).",
    "time_to_first_useful": "# of CLI invocations strictly before the first invocation that prints previously stored claim content back to the caller (replay: init → ingest → ingest → blame). Proxy for SPEC \"< 10 min\"."
  },
